<title>UK: Amoco resolves N Sea gas compression problem.</title>
<headline>Amoco resolves N Sea gas compression problem.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Amoco has resolved recent gas production problems in the southern North Sea which had pushed up prompt spot prices over the last two days, a spokesman said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>He said that there had been problems through the Indefatigable 23A platform, a compression platform, which had slowed deliveries to the beach terminal at Bacton in Norfolk, east England.</p>
<p>The company is now meeting all nominations in full and the situation is effectively resolved, he added.</p>
<p>--Sebastian Alison, London Newsroom, +44 171 542 6412</p>
</text>
